@mrdoob Maybe, I'm also not very happy about `shadowMapCullFrontFaces`. Just `shadowSide` is kinda confusing.

Maybe something like this?

``` javascript
renderer.shadowDepthMaterialSide = THREE.BackSide;
```

Or:

``` javascript
renderer.shadowMaterialSide = THREE.BackSide;
```

@rotorgames You should try to write more complete sentences, I have troubles understanding you :S. Yes, you can have a shadow of the plane, both from front and from back.

What you can't have is having shadows from non-physical objects which are invisible from one side and visible from other side. If object exists, it will cast shadow from all viewing angles.
